<BaseLayout title="Brakes & ABS Delete" description="ABS delete fittings, brake lines, proportioning valve and line lock placement, and Brembo rebuild for LS Genesis Coupe swaps.">
  <h1>Brakes &amp; ABS Delete</h1>

  <h2>ABS Delete</h2>
  <table>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Master cylinder fittings</td><td>M12x1 bubble flare</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Rest of OEM brake connections</td><td>M10x1 bubble flare</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Brake line needed</td><td>3/16" and 1/4"</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    Use any proportioning valve — it doesn't matter which master cylinder port you run to the PV. You can put a line lock before or after the PV,
    but the correct method is <strong>after the PV</strong>: it holds line pressure to the front brakes when engaged, so the rears stay free for a burnout.
  </p>
  <div class="note">
    <p><strong>Keep your odometer working:</strong> leave the ABS electrical connection plugged in. Simply unscrew the module from the ABS housing and keep it plugged in (shown in the last pictures below).</p>
  </div>
